  "cause": [
    "The hash mixer includes relocated typestr pointer bytes; fixed old.test and a.test names can share a bucket in some processes.",
    "cache_hash preserves only consecutive same-name same-flags entries. The old owner inserted ahead of the retained immortal lease separates it from the later a.test hosts record.",
    "On the second a.test insertion, cache_find_by_name constructs the temporary next chain in current hash order before rotating hash_next. With the collision, a.test(.186)->retainedlease(.1) makes .1 visible to the subsequent y.test duplicate-address check; without it, lease(.1)->a.test(.186)->end removes that address from the relevant bulk chain.",
    "The finite lease has distinct F_IMMORTAL flags and keeps x-only in both observed topologies. The immortal two-owner assertion therefore needs the noncolliding filler precondition."
  ],
